# Test accounts — dev.jobbliggaren.se

**This is the tracked TEMPLATE. Copy it to `docs/test-accounts.local.md` and fill that
copy — never this one.** The real file is gitignored because this repository is public,
and it is deliberately **not** listed in `.worktreeinclude`, so it exists only in the main
checkout. `scripts/sync-worktree-docs.ps1` refuses to copy it even if
someone lists it.

Values are filled by Klas directly on his machine. They never go into anything durable and
public: not a commit, not a PR body, not an issue, not a committed session log.

How the accounts come into existence: [`runbooks/registration-gate.md`](runbooks/registration-gate.md).
Writing one straight into the database is not the alternative; `AuthOptions` forbids it.

---

## K2 edge gate (Caddy basic-auth)

Every request to the site is challenged before it reaches the app.

- user: `<fill>`
- password: `<fill>`

The bcrypt hash of this password lives in `deploy/.env` on the box as `BASIC_AUTH_HASH`;
the plaintext exists only here.

⚠ **This credential carries a GDPR conclusion, not just access.** `release-checklist.md`'s
re-grading of the dead rights channel rests in part on the site answering `401` on every
path — so removing Basic auth, even briefly for a demo, makes that finding blocking in the
same moment, and nothing warns. Removing it is a decision, not a convenience.

